WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.890
Hybrid and cluster AI telemetry starts with understanding the full path from user request to model, data, infrastructure, policy, and response.

2
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:14.910
A production AI workflow may cross many systems before it returns an answer.

3
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:24.830
Telemetry should make that path visible enough that teams can connect user experience to model behavior, data freshness, resource pressure, and operational controls.

4
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.880
Use multiple signal types together.

5
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.170
Metrics show trends and alertable conditions.

6
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.220
Logs explain discrete events.

7
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.270
Traces connect distributed work.

8
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.730
Events and audit records capture important changes and decisions.

9
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.360
Health checks, profiles, resource telemetry, and pipeline signals complete the operating picture.

10
00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:55.330
The best telemetry design chooses signals because they answer real questions, not because a platform can emit them.

11
00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.620
Specialized AI infrastructure needs special attention.

12
00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:06.200
GPUs, accelerators, storage, queues, vector stores, retrieval indexes, model gateways, and batch pipelines can all influence reliability.

13
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:13.000
Monitor them with enough context to separate capacity, placement, data, retrieval, and model-serving issues.

14
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:20.970
At the same time, protect sensitive data through privacy-aware logging, data minimization, and governed access to telemetry.

15
00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.260
Finally, make telemetry usable during pressure.

16
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:33.400
Consistent labels, request IDs, trace IDs, model versions, cluster names, and deployment versions connect scattered signals into a path of investigation.

17
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:39.030
Alerts, SLOs, runbooks, and post-incident reviews turn telemetry into operational readiness.

18
00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.100
Good AI telemetry is not just more data.

19
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:48.340
It is disciplined evidence that helps teams act responsibly and quickly.

